# Documentation contributor checklist

A documentation-only pull request has one local path that matches CI
`fixtures-and-docs`:

```sh
uv run rocci-ops check docs
cargo test -p rocci-docs
cargo run -q -p rocci-docs -- --catalog examples/rocci/apps.toml --output dist/example-docs
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check site
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check docs
uv run rocci-ops ci fixtures-and-docs
```

`check site` / `check docs` already fail on broken links, unknown nav ids,
missing includes/assets, and duplicate routes. Staging is atomic: a failed
`rocci-docs` run keeps the previous `dist/example-docs` tree.

## Public contract

When behavior changes, update **one** canonical reference (or coverage row) in
the same change. `docs/coverage.toml` must keep every `current` and
`experimental` author-facing feature owned. `status = "removed"` stays
removed; do not relabel `@on` as current.

Do not duplicate generated `/examples/` source. Link the cataloged app.

Do not open a page with Prerequisites, Kind, Time, or difficulty badges.
Teaching pages may start with what the reader will do and close with one
Next link. Do not grow a Prerequisites course. Catalog previous/next chrome
may remain.

Do not start a user-facing page with “this page is the … guide”, “this
section is not reviewed”, “automatically generated”, or “do not copy the
file into `docs/`.” Keep coverage maps, CI commands, and “do not copy”
rules on this checklist, not on user pages.

Do not add `@page aliases` or redirects from retired academy or `/rocdown/`
routes.

Do not teach OKF or planned work as shipped. Rocdown is experimental and
lives at `/docs/rocdown/`.

Nav groups stay Start, Templates, Applications, Rocdown, Reference,
Troubleshooting, Appendix.

A new directory of listed pages needs `index.rocdown` in the same change, and
that id must appear in `docs/rocdown.toml` and `site/rocdown.toml` immediately
before the members. The sidebar landing row is Overview; do not add a second
`overview.rocdown` unless it is a distinct page. Two or more listed pages
without an index warn `RD2205`. Peel-by-id binds the first listed `…/index` as
the section landing. Nested `[[mount]]` / `[[peer]]` as used by **this**
repository (`docs/` into `site/`, `dist/example-docs` as a peer) stay here:
`source` is a directory of `.rocdown` pages, not a nested site. A missing peer
directory is skipped; links to those routes are `RD2101`. Stage
`dist/example-docs` before `rocdown check site`.

Historical News URLs return `410` at the production origin; do not encode that
table in user site docs.

Musl `--target` values and `uv run rocci-ops site` / `serve hybrid` live in
`docker/README.md`. Do not put them on the user sites page.

## Examples

Staging does not compile Roc. Cataloged standalone apps have `rocci-cli` build
tests that run when `roc` is on `PATH` (`counter_generated_app_roc_builds`,
`live_counter_generated_app_roc_builds`). Smoke `curl` lines live on each app
page. Set `ROCCI_REQUIRE_ROC=1` when Roc must not be skipped.

Example prose links into [Templates](/docs/templates/) or
[Applications](/docs/applications/), not retired tutorial URLs.

## Accessibility

`check site` does not replace a visual pass. Before merge, spot-check:

- code and tables scroll instead of overflowing the article at 320px width
- keyboard order follows the heading outline; Cmd/Ctrl-K is extra
- print and no-JavaScript still show article bodies (`:tabs` stacks)
- forced colors and `prefers-reduced-motion` do not hide text
- 200% zoom keeps nav usable

Blocking broken examples or missing canonical pages fail CI. Theme contrast
bugs belong in the Rocdown theme, not a second checker.

**Related:** [The stack](/docs/the-stack/).
Search fixtures: `docs/search-queries.toml`.
